 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by a RuntimeError being raised during duplicate registration without being wrapped in a ConflictError. The fix replaced the RuntimeError with a ConflictError in tracker/repository.py, ensuring the proper HTTP 409 status code and error code 'conflict' are returned. This change ensures that duplicate registration errors are handled correctly and surface as a 409 Conflict error instead of a 500 internal server error.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/repository.py b/tracker/repository.py\nindex 9744f5e..8411052 100644\n--- a/tracker/repository.py\n+++ b/tracker/repository.py\n@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ class UserRepository:\n                 )\n                 user_id = cur.lastrowid\n         except sqlite3.IntegrityError as exc:\n-            raise RuntimeError(\"username or email already registered\") from exc\n+            raise ConflictError(\"username or email already registered\") from exc\n         return self.get(user_id)\n \n     def get(self, user_id):\n",
